; The Dreamcast Stereo AV Cable (HKT-7400): Sega's AV OUT plug at the console end,
; three phonos at the set. The Nintendo 64 lead with a different plug script and a
; different plug: the console end is DcAvPlug, which only DcAvPort accepts, drawn as
; the moulded body (28 x 12 x 30 mm, outside the case) with the 19.4 x 5.8 mm metal
; tongue that runs 9 mm into the socket along the plug's +Z. The collision box is the
; body only, so the plug cannot be grabbed through the back panel.
;
; The console end is a SHARED end carrying all three cords -- see CompositeCable for
; why that means four plugs for three cords. Black jacket, as Sega moulded it.
[node name="DcAvCable" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_cablescript")
wire_color = Color(0.07, 0.07, 0.075, 1.0)


